    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "We are delighted to present 142 Lower Kilmacud Road to the market, a substantial four-bedroom semi-detached family home set on a generous plot in the heart of Kilmacud, Dublin 14.\n\nExtended to the rear over the years by way of twin single storey extensions, the property now offers four well-proportioned reception rooms in addition to the kitchen at ground floor level, together with a garage to the side with clear scope to extend overhead, subject to planning permission. The house is offered in need of full modernisation throughout, presenting an excellent opportunity for a purchaser to remodel and extend to their own specification, and is offered for sale with full vacant possession.\n\nAt ground floor level, the accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall, kitchen, utility storage, and four interconnecting reception rooms including the living room, dining room, garden room and a further reception room to the side, providing flexible and generous family living space throughout.\n\nUpstairs, four bedrooms are arranged off a central landing and served by a family bathroom and separate WC, offering comfortable family accommodation with further potential to reconfigure or extend, subject to planning permission.\n\nKilmacud is a well-established and highly sought-after residential area of Dublin 14, characterised by mature tree-lined streets and a strong sense of community, with Kilmacud Crokes GAA club at its heart. The location is superbly convenient, within easy reach of Stillorgan Village and Shopping Centre, the N11/M50 interchange, and the LUAS Green Line, with Kilmacud stop under 1km away (approximately a 12 minute walk), providing swift access to Dublin city centre and beyond, with a wide range of primary and secondary schools also close by. This is a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial family home with scope to extend and modernise in one of South Dublin`s most established addresses.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall\nLocated at the heart of the ground floor, providing access to all principal reception rooms and the stairs to the first floor.\n\nKitchen - 10'4\" (3.15m) x 13'4\" (4.06m)\nLarge kitchen with fitted units at base and eye level, standalone appliances will remain as part of the sale.\n\nUtility Room\nLocated off the kitchen, providing useful additional storage space.\n\nLiving Room - 11'10\" (3.61m) x 13'4\" (4.06m)\nA well-proportioned reception room to the front of the property, solid fuel fireplace.\n\nDining Room - 13'5\" (4.09m) x 12'2\" (3.71m)\nA generous reception room located centrally, ideal for family dining and also featuring a solid fuel fireplace.\n\nGarden Room - 11'7\" (3.53m) x 13'4\" (4.06m)\nLocated to the rear, overlooking the garden.\n\nReception - 12'5\" (3.78m) x 10'2\" (3.1m)\nA further reception room to the side, adjoining the garage.\n\nFirst Floor\n\nBedroom 1 - 11'2\" (3.4m) x 13'10\" (4.22m)\nA generous double bedroom to the rear, with an extensive run of fitted wardrobes and a matching dressing table and mirror unit.\n\nBedroom 2 - 11'2\" (3.4m) x 11'8\" (3.56m)\nA double bedroom to the rear, with a full run of fitted wardrobes and a dressing table with mirror.\n\nBedroom 3 - 9'0\" (2.74m) x 10'2\" (3.1m)\nDouble Bedroom\n\nBedroom 4 - 8'4\" (2.54m) x 8'8\" (2.64m)\nA single bedroom, ideal as a child`s room, home office or nursery.\n\nBathroom - 4'10\" (1.47m) x 5'5\" (1.65m)\nThe family bathroom, electric shower over bath, whb.\n\nWC\nA separate WC located off the landing.\n\nOutside\n\nFront\nOff-street parking is provided to the front, with access to the attached garage offering further parking and storage, and scope to extend overhead, subject to planning permission.\n\nRear\nA private, directly south facing rear garden lies beyond the twin single storey extensions to the ground floor, offering further outdoor amenity space.\n\nNotice\nThese particulars are issued by Mark Kelly & Associates (MKA) on the understanding that all negotiations are conducted through us. They are provided in good faith for guidance only and do not form part of any offer or contract. MKA has not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, services or equipment, and purchasers must satisfy themselves as to their condition and working order. All descriptions, measurements, dimensions, maps, plans, photographs, condition, permissions, licences, access, prices, rents, outgoings and other information are approximate, for guidance only and may be subject to change without notice. Maps and plans are not to scale. Photographs are provided for presentation and guidance purposes. Where appropriate, AI-assisted enhancement, refinement or virtual furnishing may be used to improve presentation or assist purchasers in visualising layout, scale or potential. Such imagery is not intended to materially alter or misrepresent the structure, layout, condition or features of the property. Neither MKA nor its staff or representatives have authority to make or give any representation or warranty in relation to the property.\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Four bedroom semi-detached family home. </li><li> Garage to side with scope to extend above, subject to planning permission. </li><li> Twin single storey extensions to the rear. </li><li> Four reception rooms at ground floor level. </li><li> South Facing rear garden. </li><li> Gas fired central heating. </li><li> Double glazed windows throughout. </li><li> Sold with full vacant possession. </li><li> Offered in need of modernisation. </li><li> Built in 1951</li></ul>"
      },
